/-!
# `GX.BTZ.HeadlineBridge` — the bridge of the headline (DEC-119)

Package WP-46g. Infrastructure for the headline of `papers/gx` §4.6
(`theo:globally_hyperbolic_cauchy_complete_cauchy_maximal`, `RamcovGX.tex:2363`), as ruled by
**DEC-119** (2026-11-03, "Bridge"). **No ledger label is certified here, so nothing is marked**:
the headline's two halves live on two presentations of an `𝔼₀`-manifold `M` — the charted one
(`ChartedSpace E0Y M`, `HasGroupoid M e0Groupoid`, on which Cauchy-compactness, Cauchy-maximality
and the developing pairs `(𝒟, ρ)` of `Reg M = e0RegMFlat M` are stated, `GXScaffold.BTZ.AbsMax`,
`GXScaffold.BTZ.Uniformization`) and the singular one (`SingularGXStructure`, DEC-25, on which the
maximal branched covering `M̃` and its BTZ data `GX.BTZTildeData` are built, `GX.BTZ.Manifolds`).
This file builds the three bridges DEC-119 asks for, **0 `sorry`**:

* **(1) the singular structure** — `GX.E0Bridge.e0SingularGXStructure`: the maximal a.e.
  `(Isom 𝐌³, 𝐌³)`-atlas generated (`cor:maximal_atlas`) by the *flat charts*
  `GX.E0Bridge.flatCharts` (a chart of `M` into `𝕄 ⊕ 𝔼₀` followed by a regular chart of the
  model). Its regular locus is `Reg M` (`GX.E0Bridge.reg_e0SingularGXStructure`), its singular
  locus `sing₀(M)` (`GX.E0Bridge.sing_e0SingularGXStructure`); the inclusion `Reg ⊆ e0RegM` is the
  model fact `GX.btz_sing` transported through the `𝔼₀`-chart (`GX.E0Bridge.source_subset_e0RegM`).
  Every singular point is the centre of an `𝔼₀`-chart of `def:atlas`
  (`GX.E0Bridge.isBTZSingModelled_e0`), so `M` is an `𝔼₀`-manifold in the sense of
  `GX.IsBTZSingModelled` and `GX.BTZTildeData` exists over it. `Reg M` is portly
  (`GX.E0Bridge.isPortly_e0RegM`).
* **(2) `reg M̃ ≃ₜ` the universal cover of `Reg M`** — `GX.E0Bridge.regTildeHomeo`, over `M`
  (`GX.E0Bridge.proj_regTildeHomeo`) and on base points (`GX.E0Bridge.regTildeHomeo_symm_base`),
  onto `lean-causal`'s `Causal.UniversalCover (e0RegMFlat M)` — the type the headline
  `GX.btz_uniformization_C1` quantifies its developing pairs over; gx's form
  `GX.E0Bridge.regTildeHomeoGX` (`prop:universality`'s `\widetilde{Y∖S} ↪ \widetilde Y^S`).
* **(3) `𝒟` extended to the BTZ points** — `GX.E0Bridge.exists_dev_extension`: for every
  `\widetilde M`-datum `d` and every developing pair `(𝒟, ρ)` of `Reg M`, an isometry `g` with
  `g · d.D` `T_BTZ`-continuous on `M̃` and equal to `𝒟` on `reg M̃`; datum forms
  `GX.E0Bridge.exists_btzTildeData_extending` (same `T_BTZ`, developing map `= 𝒟` on `reg M̃`) and
  `GX.E0Bridge.exists_btzTildeData_of_isDevelopingPair` (the datum exists). Conversely the
  developing map of every datum is, with a holonomy, a developing pair of `Reg M`
  (`GX.E0Bridge.exists_isDevelopingPair_devOnCover`, from `GX.E0Bridge.isGXMorphism_devOnCover`).

Proved here, of general use: `GX.E0Bridge.univCoverCongr` (universal covers of equal subsets),
`GX.E0Bridge.isRegDevelopingOnReg_smul`, `GX.E0Bridge.btzTildeDataSmul` (a datum translated by
`Isom(𝐌³)`), `GX.E0Bridge.eventually_dev_eq_smul` (the local form of a regular developing map of
`M̃`: a translate of a flat chart read through `p`).

## Hypothesis checklist

| DEC-119 / the bridge | here |
|---|---|
| `M` an `𝔼₀`-manifold (`ChartedSpace E0Y M`, `HasGroupoid M e0Groupoid`) | ✓ the only hypotheses of (1) |
| `Reg`/`Sing` of the new structure match | ✓ `= e0RegM M`, `= chartedSing e0SingY M 0` |
| `M̃` (`MaxBranchedCover (Sing M) y₀`) | carried for (2)/(3): `M` Hausdorff, first countable, connected (`maxBranched_basic`'s hypotheses; local path-connectedness is derived from the charts) |
| `reg M̃ ≃ₜ \widetilde{Reg M}` | ✓ homeomorphism, natural topology of `M̃`, over `M` |
| `𝒟` "extended continuously to the BTZ points" | ✓ continuous for `T_BTZ` (`BTZTildeData.T'`, DEC-106: the final homeomorphism's topology); for the natural topology only on `reg M̃` (`GX.E0Bridge.continuousAt_dev`) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* (a) `FirstCountableTopology M` is carried for (2)–(3) (it is a hypothesis of
  `GX.maxBranched_basic`); it holds for every `𝔼₀`-manifold but is not derived here (`E0Y` has no
  `FirstCountableTopology` instance at this pin).
* (b) Uniqueness of the extension in (3) is not stated: `reg M̃` need not be `T_BTZ`-dense from
  the fields of `BTZTildeData` alone.
* (c) Beyond DEC-119's list, built because the headline needs it to use `GX.BTZ.Manifolds`
  (§4): the causality `GX.e0ManifoldCausality M isBTZSingModelled_e0` (generated by the a.e.
  atlas and the `𝔼₀`-charts) **is** the charted causality `Causal.CBG.chartedCausality E0LM.D M`
  the headline's GH hypothesis is read for (`GX.E0Bridge.e0ManifoldCausality_eq_chartedCausality`,
  `GX.E0Bridge.globallyHyperbolic_e0ManifoldCausality_iff`), through a general lemma
  (`GX.E0Bridge.chartAtlasCausality_eq_chartedCausality`: an atlas compatible with the preferred
  one generates the charted causality). Every base point `x₀` of `e0RegMFlat M` is
  `regPtF (basePt x₀)` (`GX.E0Bridge.regPtF_basePt`, `rfl`).

